UID:translation-house-looren-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260901T123517Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261015
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261016
SUMMARY:Deadline: Translation House Looren: Translators' Residencies and Pr
 o Helvetia Stipends 2027
DESCRIPTION:Translators' residency at Uebersetzerhaus Looren in Wernetshaus
 en near Zurich. Looren offers a free residency for literary translators wi
 th a current contract\, including six competitive CHF 4\,000 stipend grant
 s per year tied to one-month residencies. The Pro Helvetia residency progr
 amme (separately funded) has a 2026-10-15 deadline for 2027 stays. The Jam
 es Joyce Scholarship and Looren Residency 2027 closes 2026-10-31. General 
 free residencies are accepted on a rolling basis throughout the year. ELIG
 IBILITY: literary translators with substantial published work and a curren
 t translation contract\; any language combination is welcome. Apply via th
 e application page on looren.net. No application fee.\n\nOrganisation: Ueb
 ersetzerhaus Looren\nLocation: Wernetshausen\, Switzerland (Zurich region)
 \nAward: Free residency stay (apartments at the translation house). Six co
 mpetitive CHF 4\,000 translation grants per year\, each tied to a one-mont
 h residency. Pro Helvetia residency programme separately funded. James Joy
 ce Scholarship and Looren Residency 2027 has its own conditions. No applic
 ation fee.\nDuration: Stays of typically 2 weeks to 2 months\; CHF 4\,000 
 stipend grants tied to one-month residencies\n\nMore: https://looren.net/e
 n/residencies/application-for-a-stay?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk
 &utm_medium=referral
URL:https://looren.net/en/residencies/application-for-a-stay?utm_source=art
 ificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Wernetshausen\, Switzerland (Zurich region)
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:jan-michalski-foundation-residency-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260901T123517Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260831
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260901
SUMMARY:Deadline: Jan Michalski Foundation: Writers Residency 2027
DESCRIPTION:Residency for writers and translators at the Jan Michalski Foun
 dation in Montricher\, Switzerland\, set in seven distinctive 'cabin' modu
 les hanging from an openwork canopy\, offering conditions to start\, conti
 nue or finish a writing project. Around forty authors from around the worl
 d (emerging to established) are hosted each year. Open to all kinds of wri
 ting and all languages\, with priority given to literary writers and trans
 lators\; other disciplines are welcome as long as literature is at the hea
 rt of the project. Residencies are for individuals or pairs working on a c
 ommon project (e.g. a writer and a translator). A percentage of residencie
 s are dedicated to nature writing. WHAT IS PROVIDED: a private cabin for i
 ndependent living (a separate cabin per person for pairs\; one accessible 
 cabin for reduced mobility)\, travel costs to and from home\, a weekly all
 owance of CHF 400\, breakfast and lunch\, electric bikes\, and daytime lib
 rary access. ELIGIBILITY: no age or nationality restrictions\; beginners a
 ccepted\; one application per year\; former residents may not reapply (fam
 ilies\, children and pets cannot be accommodated). Stays cannot be split i
 nto multiple periods. Selection is by a panel chaired by Vera Michalski-Ho
 ffmann\, assessing the literary quality of the project\, the candidate's b
 ackground\, and whether the stay length matches the project scope. APPLICA
 TION: online in English or French (work excerpts may be in any language)\;
  the 2027 form is open 2 June to 31 August 2026\; selected candidates anno
 unced December 2026.\n\nOrganisation: Jan Michalski Foundation for Writing
  and Literature\nLocation: Montricher\, Switzerland (Swiss Jura\, near Lau
 sanne and Geneva)\nAward: Weekly allowance of CHF 400\, plus travel costs 
 to and from home covered\, accommodation in a private cabin\, and breakfas
 t and lunch provided. Electric bikes and library access included.\nDuratio
 n: Two weeks to three months (first 2027 residents arrive mid-January 2027
 )\n\nMore: https://fondation-janmichalski.com/en/residences?utm_source=art
 ificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://fondation-janmichalski.com/en/residences?utm_source=artificialn
 ouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Montricher\, Switzerland (Swiss Jura\, near Lausanne and Geneva)
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:hkbu-iww-writers-in-residence-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260901T123517Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260814
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260815
SUMMARY:Deadline: Hong Kong Baptist University: International Writers' Work
 shop 2027 (Writers-in-Residence)
DESCRIPTION:International Writers' Workshop (IWW) at Hong Kong Baptist Univ
 ersity (HKBU)\, founded in 2004\, has hosted over 150 writers from more th
 an 60 countries. The 2027 Writers-in-Residence Programme runs 26 February 
 to 25 March 2027 and culminates in the IWW Literary Festival on the theme 
 'Inheritance'. Writers are encouraged to share a piece of writing in conve
 rsation with the festival theme. ELIGIBILITY: have at least one published 
 book\; currently reside outside of Hong Kong\; have a functional command o
 f English or Chinese (Mandarin or Cantonese). WHAT IWW PROVIDES: round-tri
 p economy class airfare\; accommodation on HKBU's campus for 4 weeks\; a p
 er diem. DEADLINE: 14 August 2026. APPLY via the IWW HKBU call for applica
 tion (PDF).\n\nOrganisation: International Writers' Workshop (IWW)\, Hong 
 Kong Baptist University (HKBU)\nLocation: HKBU campus\, Hong Kong\nAward: 
 Round-trip economy class airfare\; accommodation on HKBU's campus for 4 we
 eks\; a per diem. No application fee.\nDuration: 4-week residency\, 26 Feb
 ruary to 25 March 2027\, culminating in the IWW Literary Festival on the t
 heme 'Inheritance'\n\nMore: https://iww.hkbu.edu.hk/?utm_source=artificial
 nouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://iww.hkbu.edu.hk/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medi
 um=referral
LOCATION:HKBU campus\, Hong Kong
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:oif-artist-mobility-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260901T123517Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260831
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260901
SUMMARY:Deadline: OIF: Support for Artist Mobility and Circulation of Cultu
 ral Goods 2026 (Francophonie)
DESCRIPTION:The OIF Support for Artist Mobility and Circulation of Cultural
  Goods programme provides grants of up to EUR 5\,000 for mobility (travel\
 , accommodation\, visa fees\, logistics) and up to EUR 2\,500 for circulat
 ion of cultural goods (excess baggage\, freight\, customs) within the Fran
 cophone zone\; both can be combined. ELIGIBILITY: professional artists and
  established artistic collectives with a demonstrated connection to the Fr
 ancophone space (by nationality\, working language\, or artistic collabora
 tions)\, residing in an OIF member state\, with minimum 2 years of experie
 nce in the cultural or artistic sector\; must directly manage the project 
 (not act as intermediaries)\; one application per individual per call. ELI
 GIBLE DISCIPLINES: live performance (music\, theatre\, dance\, comedy\, st
 orytelling)\, cinema/audiovisual\, literature/publishing\, and visual arts
 . PRIORITY given to projects promoting gender equality\, women artists\, c
 reators under 35\, and South-South mobility. Projects must take place betw
 een 25 March and 30 November 2026. Multiple selection sessions throughout 
 the year\; call open until 31 August 2026. Information webinars: 11 March\
 , 13 May\, and 8 July 2026 at 3 PM Paris time. Contact: culture.dlc@franco
 phonie.org. Apply at https://appelsaprojets.francophonie.org/fr/applicatio
 ns/soutien-a-la-circulation-des-biens-et-mobilite-des-artistes.\n\nOrganis
 ation: Organisation internationale de la Francophonie (OIF)\nLocation: Fra
 ncophone zone (OIF member states globally)\nAward: Up to EUR 5\,000 for ar
 tist mobility (travel\, accommodation\, visas\, logistics). Up to EUR 2\,5
 00 for circulation of cultural goods (excess baggage\, freight\, customs).
  Both can be combined. No application fee.\nDuration: Residencies or tours
  of 5 days to 3 months. Projects must take place between 25 March and 30 N
 ovember 2026.\n\nMore: https://appelsaprojets.francophonie.org/fr/applicat
 ions/soutien-a-la-circulation-des-biens-et-mobilite-des-artistes?utm_sourc
 e=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://appelsaprojets.francophonie.org/fr/applications/soutien-a-la-ci
 rculation-des-biens-et-mobilite-des-artistes?utm_source=artificialnouveaug
 rantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Francophone zone (OIF member states globally)
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:prohelvetia-writing-in-residency-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260901T123517Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260901
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260902
SUMMARY:Deadline: Writing in Residency
DESCRIPTION:Pro Helvetia's Writing in Residency programme provides residenc
 y opportunities (for example Traduki in Southeast Europe or Art Omi) for a
 uthors and translators to develop or research projects. Applicants must ha
 ve prior professionally published work. ELIGIBILITY: requires a connection
  to Switzerland (Swiss citizenship\, or permanent residency with regular a
 rtistic activity in Switzerland)\; not open to practitioners without a Swi
 ss connection. WHAT IS OFFERED: travel and accommodation costs (varying by
  destination)\, plus childcare support of up to CHF 1\,000 per month for a
 pplicants with caregiving responsibilities. Submission deadline 1 Septembe
 r (23:59 CEST). Apply via the Pro Helvetia portal.\n\nOrganisation: Pro He
 lvetia (Swiss Arts Council)\nLocation: Switzerland-based authors and trans
 lators\; residencies at partner locations abroad (e.g. Traduki in Southeas
 t Europe\, Art Omi).\nAward: Travel and accommodation costs (vary by desti
 nation)\; childcare support up to CHF 1\,000 per month for applicants with
  caregiving responsibilities. No application fee.\nDuration: Residency to 
 develop or research a project\; deadline 1 September.\n\nMore: https://pro
 helvetia.ch/en/find-support/writing-in-residency?utm_source=artificialnouv
 eaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://prohelvetia.ch/en/find-support/writing-in-residency?utm_source=
 artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Switzerland-based authors and translators\; residencies at partner
  locations abroad (e.g. Traduki in Southeast Europe\, Art Omi).
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:wheeler-centre-next-chapter-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260901T123517Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260731
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260801
SUMMARY:Deadline: The Wheeler Centre: The Next Chapter 2027
DESCRIPTION:The Next Chapter is The Wheeler Centre's flagship writing progr
 am\, designed to elevate Australian stories that are underrepresented and 
 to nurture a new wave of writers to tell them. Each fellow receives a AUD 
 $15\,000 stipend and is paired with a handpicked mentor for a twelve-month
  period to progress a major writing project. Fellows also receive a reside
 ncy at Varuna\, The National Writers' House\; an end-of-year publishing in
 tensive at The Wheeler Centre\; and meaningful opportunities to connect wi
 th peers\, agents\, publishers\, and readers. One fellowship place is dedi
 cated specifically to a poet: The Malcolm Robertson Fellowship. 2027 judge
 s: Melissa Lucashenko\, Micaela Sahhar\, Cher Tan\, and Melanie Saward. EL
 IGIBILITY: Australian writers. No specific genre restrictions stated\; the
  program focuses on stories that are not currently being told and voices t
 hat are underrepresented. TIMELINE: submissions open 2 June 2026\; submiss
 ions close 31 July 2026 (5pm)\; 2027 Next Chapter Fellows announced 10 Nov
 ember 2026. Questions: thenextchapter@wheelercentre.com. Apply at https://
 www.wheelercentre.com/the-next-chapter.\n\nOrganisation: The Wheeler Centr
 e\nLocation: Melbourne\, Australia\; includes residency at Varuna\, The Na
 tional Writers' House\, and an end-of-year publishing intensive at The Whe
 eler Centre.\nAward: AUD $15\,000 stipend per fellow. No application fee.\
 nDuration: 12 months.\n\nMore: https://www.wheelercentre.com/the-next-chap
 ter?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.wheelercentre.com/the-next-chapter?utm_source=artificialnou
 veaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Melbourne\, Australia\; includes residency at Varuna\, The Nationa
 l Writers' House\, and an end-of-year publishing intensive at The Wheeler 
 Centre.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ucross-fellowship-native-american-writers-spring-2027@artificialnouveau
 .github.io
DTSTAMP:20260901T123517Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260715
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260716
SUMMARY:Deadline: Ucross Fellowship for Native American Writers: Spring 202
 7
DESCRIPTION:The Ucross Fellowship for Native American Writers is a dedicate
 d fellowship within Ucross Foundation's residency program\, offering fully
  funded time and space to write on a working cattle ranch in the foothills
  of Wyoming's Bighorn Mountains. The fellowship provides living accommodat
 ions\, meals\, and work space at no charge\, with no application fee. One 
 Fellowship winner is selected per session\; all applicants also have the o
 ption of being considered for a general Ucross residency. ELIGIBILITY: ope
 n to Native American writers who are practicing contemporary writers curre
 ntly producing work in one or more genres\, including but not limited to f
 iction\, nonfiction\, poetry\, drama\, screenwriting\, playwriting\, and h
 ybrid forms\; and who are enrolled members of a state-recognized or federa
 lly-recognized Tribe\, Pueblo\, Nation\, Native Community\, Political Enti
 ty\, or Alaskan Native Village. The work sample and project description ar
 e the most significant features of the application. Unless the work is gen
 uinely interdisciplinary (the genres interconnect)\, applicants are encour
 aged to apply in a single primary discipline and submit a work sample and 
 project description emphasizing that discipline. Work-sample requirements:
  FICTION\, 20 pages of double-spaced fiction (a novel excerpt\, a story\, 
 several stories\, or a combination)\; NONFICTION\, 20 pages of double-spac
 ed nonfiction\; POETRY\, 10 pages of poetry (may be single-spaced)\; PLAYW
 RITING\, one complete play (production documentation may be included if re
 levant)\, noting the 20 pages for reviewers to read\; SCREENWRITING\, one 
 complete screenplay (production documentation may be included if relevant)
 \, noting the 20 pages for reviewers to read. All writing samples should i
 nclude your full name. The open call for the Spring 2027 session closes Ju
 ly 15\, 2026 (apply by 11:59 p.m. MT). A separate Ucross Fellowship for Na
 tive American Visual Artists is also offered.\n\nOrganisation: Ucross Foun
 dation\nLocation: Sheridan\, Wyoming\, USA\nAward: Fully funded fellowship
  residency\; living accommodations\, meals\, and work space provided. No a
 pplication fee.\nDuration: Spring session (February through early June 202
 7)\; residencies range from two to six weeks\n\nMore: https://www.ucrossfo
 undation.org/residency-program.html?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&
 utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.ucrossfoundation.org/residency-program.html?utm_source=arti
 ficialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Sheridan\, Wyoming\, USA
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:albee-foundation-barn-residency-winter-spring-2027@artificialnouveau.gi
 thub.io
DTSTAMP:20260901T123517Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260914
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260915
SUMMARY:Deadline: Edward F. Albee Foundation: William Flanagan Memorial Cre
 ative Persons Center Residency (Winter/Spring 2027)
DESCRIPTION:Edward Albee founded this foundation in 1962 with the proceeds 
 from Who's Afraid of Virginia Woolf?\, and it has run The Barn in Montauk 
 for close to sixty years as a place for writers and visual artists to get 
 uninterrupted time. The house sits on a secluded knoll and takes four resi
 dents at a time\, usually two writers and two visual artists\, each with a
 n en-suite bedroom and a separate studio. The environment is deliberately 
 simple and communal: residents share responsibility for the space and are 
 expected to work seriously and keep it quiet for everyone else. ELIGIBILIT
 Y: any creative person over 18\, any nationality\, students included\; sel
 ection uses talent and need as the only criteria. There are no fees at all
 \, to apply or to stay. Domestic Fellows get a USD 2\,500 stipend on compl
 eting the residency\; international Fellows get expenses reimbursed up to 
 USD 2\,500. DATES: this cycle covers residencies from January to June 2027
 . Applications open at 08:00 on 17 August 2026 and close on 14 September 2
 026\, through apply.albeefoundation.org. The next cycle (July-November 202
 7) opens 11 January 2027 and closes 15 February 2027. The Barn is closed e
 very December. Contact apply@albeefoundation.org or (212) 226-2020.\n\nOrg
 anisation: The Edward F. Albee Foundation\nLocation: Montauk\, Long Island
 \, New York\, USA (about two miles from downtown Montauk and the Atlantic)
 \nAward: Fully funded residency: private en-suite bedroom and separate wor
 king studio\, USD 2\,500 stipend for domestic Fellows paid on successful c
 ompletion\, or reimbursement of expenses capped at USD 2\,500 for internat
 ional Fellows. No application fee and no residency fee.\nDuration: One ful
 l calendar month between January and June 2027\; partial months are not of
 fered\n\nMore: https://apply.albeefoundation.org/?utm_source=artificialnou
 veaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://apply.albeefoundation.org/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdes
 k&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Montauk\, Long Island\, New York\, USA (about two miles from downt
 own Montauk and the Atlantic)
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:tartu-city-of-literature-residency-autumn-2026@artificialnouveau.github
 .io
DTSTAMP:20260901T123517Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260901
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260902
SUMMARY:Deadline: Tartu UNESCO City of Literature Residency for Writers and
  Translators\, Autumn 2026
DESCRIPTION:The Estonian Literary Society\, which coordinates Tartu UNESCO 
 City of Literature\, runs an international residency programme for writers
  and translators that has hosted authors from Slovenia\, Ireland\, Hungary
 \, the USA\, the UK\, Ukraine and Canada since 2017. This is the open call
  for the autumn 2026 slot: one resident stays two months in the Karl Risti
 kivi residency apartment in Tartu\, working on their own writing or transl
 ation while connecting with the local literary scene. WHAT THE RESIDENCY O
 FFERS: a EUR 600 monthly stipend\, travel reimbursement up to EUR 350\, fr
 ee accommodation\, a local support coordinator to help arrange cultural en
 gagements\, and opportunities to perform and present at literary events. T
 he autumn period covers the interdisciplinary literary festival Crazy Tart
 u on 12 to 14 November\, and the resident is offered a slot to perform the
 re alongside writers\, poets\, musicians and artists from Estonia and abro
 ad. ELIGIBILITY: open to writers\, poets and translators of Estonian liter
 ature of any nationality\; applicants need an upper-intermediate level of 
 spoken English\, at least one published book\, screenplay\, theatre script
  or translation from Estonian into another language\, a demonstrable inter
 est in Estonian culture and literature\, a willingness to take part in loc
 al literary activities\, and a commitment to working on their own literary
  project during the stay. HOW TO APPLY: complete the online application fo
 rm linked from the residency page and upload a fragment of up to five page
 s of a published text (in Estonian or English) or of a published translati
 on. SELECTION: made by a committee representing the Estonian Literary Soci
 ety\, the Estonian Writers Union\, the Estonian Literary Museum and the Ta
 rtu Literature House Foundation. Results are announced before 15 September
  2026. The programme's stated aims are to enhance international exchange\,
  diversify the local literary scene\, introduce new foreign authors and th
 eir work to Estonian readers\, and build lasting connections beyond the re
 sidency period. Questions: Marja Unt\, eks@kirjandus.ee. Deadline 1 Septem
 ber 2026.\n\nOrganisation: Estonian Literary Society (Eesti Kirjanduse Sel
 ts)\, Focal Point for Tartu UNESCO City of Literature\nLocation: Tartu\, E
 stonia. Open to writers\, poets and translators of Estonian literature wor
 ldwide.\nAward: Monthly stipend of EUR 600 for the two-month stay (EUR 1\,
 200 in total)\, plus reimbursement of travel costs up to EUR 350. Free acc
 ommodation is provided in the Karl Ristikivi residency apartment\, which h
 as a bedroom\, living room\, kitchen\, bathroom and exhibition room. One r
 esident is selected. No application fee.\nDuration: Two months\, 15 Octobe
 r to 15 December 2026\, with some flexibility on exact dates\n\nMore: http
 s://tartu.kirjandus.ee/residency-autumn-2026?utm_source=artificialnouveaug
 rantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://tartu.kirjandus.ee/residency-autumn-2026?utm_source=artificialn
 ouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Tartu\, Estonia. Open to writers\, poets and translators of Estoni
 an literature worldwide.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:archipel-butor-livre-de-dialogue-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260901T123517Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260830
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260831
SUMMARY:Deadline: Archipel Butor Livre de dialogue Creation Residency 2027
DESCRIPTION:Archipel Butor runs its creation residency out of the former ho
 me of the writer Michel Butor in Lucinges\, Haute-Savoie\, and this call i
 s for a livre de dialogue\, a dialogue book made jointly by a writer and a
  visual artist. The residency exists to give a pair concentrated time to d
 evelop a book together and to raise the profile of artist book culture and
  of collaboration at the centre of artistic process. WHO APPLIES: a pair m
 ade up of an author with a project for a dialogue book and a visual artist
  collaborating on it. The two do not need to have worked together before\,
  but both must be present during the shared periods. WHAT IS PROVIDED: EUR
  2\,000 gross per month per artist\, up to two return trips per person wit
 hin France and Europe\, and accommodation in the writer's house. STRUCTURE
 : two months in total\, taken as eight weeks which may be split across the
  year from January 2027\, with 70 percent of the time given to creation an
 d 30 percent to mediation and public engagement activities. A videoconfere
 nce is held with the selected laureates beforehand to arrange on-site sche
 duling and the mediation sessions. HOW TO APPLY: follow the official call 
 document downloadable from the residency page\, submitting a single PDF to
  accueil@archipel-butor.fr containing a joint letter\, biographies of both
  practitioners\, the artistic proposal\, technical specifications and the 
 proposed mediation activities. NOTE: the call and application file are in 
 French. Deadline 30 August 2026.\n\nOrganisation: Archipel Butor\nLocation
 : Lucinges (74380)\, Haute-Savoie\, France\, in the house of the writer Mi
 chel Butor.\nAward: Creation grant of EUR 2\,000 gross per month per artis
 t\, so roughly EUR 4\,000 each across the two months and EUR 8\,000 for th
 e pair. Up to two return journeys per person are covered within France and
  Europe. Accommodation is provided in Michel Butor's writer's house. No ap
 plication fee.\nDuration: Two months in total\, taken as eight weeks that 
 may be split\, starting from January 2027. Time is split 70 percent creati
 on and 30 percent mediation activities.\n\nMore: https://www.archipel-buto
 r.fr/residence-creation/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=
 referral
URL:https://www.archipel-butor.fr/residence-creation/?utm_source=artificial
 nouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Lucinges (74380)\, Haute-Savoie\, France\, in the house of the wri
 ter Michel Butor.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:les-antipodes-numeric-2026-the-word@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260901T123517Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260908
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260909
SUMMARY:Deadline: Numeric 2026: The Word (Les antipodes Research and Creati
 on Residency)
DESCRIPTION:Two research and creation residency grants in Agullana\, Catalo
 nia\, for artists\, thinkers and scientists of any branch (formal\, natura
 l\, social\, applied) working at the intersection of art\, culture\, scien
 ce and thought. THIS YEAR'S THEME\, The Word\, is squarely about large lan
 guage models. The framework moves from the word as creative principle acro
 ss traditions (the Judeo-Christian creating God\, the Quran as uncreated w
 ord\, the Sanskrit Om and the Vedas\, mantras that summon rather than desc
 ribe) to science relocating that intuition in the cell (Sagan's four-lette
 r alphabet of DNA as a material text\, Margulis countering that the langua
 ge of life is chemistry\, Witzany holding that all cell interactions are s
 ign-mediated)\, and then to LLMs\, which for the first time detach the wor
 d from the flesh and generate text through a probabilistic architecture tr
 ained on human language. The call asks what LLMs reveal about authorship\,
  originality and meaning when a system generates text that moves\, persuad
 es or deceives without experience or intention\, and whether we can still 
 say the models operate exclusively on human experience once they ingest th
 eir own output. It explicitly wants work that blurs comprehension and simu
 lation\, authorship and recombination\, and it names antecedents worth kno
 wing before applying: Ramon Llull's Ars Magna\, Joan Brossa's Sextina cibe
 rnetica\, Oulipo constraint writing\, oracles and divination\, oral-formul
 aic transmission\, translation as probabilistic approximation\, exquisite 
 corpses\, Burroughs's cut-ups\, automatic writing\, musical improvisation 
 and scientific simulation. Les antipodes asks for engagement 'beyond the i
 nstrumental use of the tools' and away from utopian and dystopian framings
 . WHAT YOU GET: spacious\, luminous\, independent work spaces plus a share
 d terrace in the centre of the village\, spaces for meeting\, dialogue and
  public presentation\, introductions to local\, academic\, artistic and pr
 ofessional contacts on request\, and support organising any activities tha
 t arise. The residency ends with an informal presentation\, and results ma
 y feed into the publications or public programme of Les antipodes. IMPORTA
 NTLY\, this is not an acquisition prize and involves no transfer of rights
 : authorship and intellectual property stay with the creators\, and select
 ion implies no acquisition of the work. Credits on resulting work must ack
 nowledge Numeric 2026 and its collaborators. WHO CAN APPLY: open to everyo
 ne of legal age\, any discipline or origin\, individually or as a collecti
 ve\, with the stipend shared among collective members. Applications must b
 e in Catalan or English whatever the working language of the project\, sub
 mitted through the online form with an optional PDF of up to 5 pages and 1
 0 MB. One application per person or collective. EVALUATION\, in order of w
 eight: singularity and innovation\; relevance to this year's LLM framework
 \; and interaction and transfer of value\, meaning relations with the soci
 al and geographical environment of Agullana and the Emporda and a plan for
  presenting the outcome in editorial\, on-site\, performative\, sound\, au
 diovisual or other form. The call may be declared void if no proposal reac
 hes the required level. PRACTICAL: residents must hold their own health co
 ver (EHIC for EU citizens\, or valid travel or health insurance for Spain 
 otherwise) and are responsible for their own equipment. Supported by the G
 eneralitat de Catalunya\, Agullana and Figueres town councils\, and Accion
  Cultural Espanola through the PICE national residencies programme. Terms 
 are published in Arabic\, Catalan\, English\, Spanish\, French and Chinese
 .\n\nOrganisation: Les antipodes\, with Bolit Centre d'Art Contemporani Gi
 rona and Museu de l'Emporda Figueres\nLocation: Agullana\, Alt Emporda\, C
 atalonia\, Spain. A village of 900 people\, 20 km from Figueres and the Vi
 lafant high-speed rail station\, 40 km from Perpignan\, 60 km from Girona\
 , 160 km from Barcelona.\nAward: Two grants. Each provides a stipend of EU
 R 1\,000 as taxable base (taxes and withholdings apply)\, round-trip trave
 l within the European Union\, and accommodation and meals for the four wee
 ks in Agullana. Travel and meals cover the resident only\, though the shar
 ed apartment can host immediate family by arrangement. Numeric also provid
 es the resources specified in the application and agreed during preparatio
 n. No application fee. Note that if a selected candidate lacks the profess
 ional registration needed to receive the stipend and payment has to be arr
 anged through Les antipodes\, the resulting costs are deducted from the st
 ipend.\nDuration: Four weeks\, 2 to 30 November 2026\, with both residenci
 es running simultaneously. Preceded by one month of preparation and follow
 ed by a two-month closing period. Applications 23 July to 8 September 2026
 \; decision announced 22 September 2026.\n\nMore: https://lesantipodes.com
 /numeric/2026_bases_en.html?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medi
 um=referral
URL:https://lesantipodes.com/numeric/2026_bases_en.html?utm_source=artifici
 alnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Agullana\, Alt Emporda\, Catalonia\, Spain. A village of 900 peopl
 e\, 20 km from Figueres and the Vilafant high-speed rail station\, 40 km f
 rom Perpignan\, 60 km from Girona\, 160 km from Barcelona.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:granada-unesco-writers-in-residence-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260901T123517Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260906
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260907
SUMMARY:Deadline: International Granada Writers in Residence Programme 2026
DESCRIPTION:A 30-night residency in Granada for two writers\, run by Granad
 a UNESCO City of Literature with the University of Granada. OPEN TO WRITER
 S RESIDING IN ANY COUNTRY AND WRITING IN ANY LANGUAGE\, which makes this o
 ne of the more genuinely international literary residencies. The programme
  exists to build connections between writers from Granada and writers worl
 dwide\, support the internationalisation of writers associated with Granad
 a\, strengthen the international links of the city's literary ecosystem\, 
 and promote Granada as a welcoming destination for creative talent. ELIGIB
 ILITY: applicants must have published AT LEAST TWO INDIVIDUALLY AUTHORED B
 OOKS. Contributions to anthologies or collective volumes do not count\, se
 lf-published works are not eligible\, and chapbooks (plaquettes) are not c
 ounted as books. Eligible genres are novels\, essays\, poetry\, drama and 
 hybrid literary forms. An intermediate to advanced level of English and/or
  Spanish is required\, along with a synopsis of the literary project to be
  developed during the residency. TREATED AS AN ASSET BUT NOT MANDATORY: kn
 owledge of Spanish at any level\, an interest in the cultural and historic
 al heritage of Granada\, an extract from a published book translated into 
 Spanish or English running 1\,500 to 3\,000 words\, and one or more letter
 s of recommendation. OBLIGATIONS: residents devote the period to their lit
 erary project\, take part in the public activities and community engagemen
 t the programme organises\, and publicly acknowledge the stay. They may no
 t undertake public activities with other institutions or in other cities w
 ithout prior notification and authorisation from the organisers. APPLYING:
  complete the application form\, a PDF that must be opened in Adobe Acroba
 t\, and email it to talleres@granadaciudaddeliteratura.com. Incomplete for
 ms are treated as invalid. A committee of experts appointed jointly by Gra
 nada UNESCO City of Literature and the University of Granada decides. Past
  residents give a sense of the level: Kirsty Logan and Petra Zist (2017)\,
  Sahar Delijani and Aleksandra Lipczak (2018)\, Luciana Jazmin Coronado an
 d Marli Roode (2019)\, Paulina Flores and Iosi Havilio (2021)\, Taimi Dieg
 uez and Frank Westerman (2022)\, Nell Leyshon and Yuliana Ortiz Ruano (202
 3)\, Karina Sainz Borgo and James Womack (2024)\, Ahlam Bsharat and Nikki 
 Dekker (2025).\n\nOrganisation: Granada UNESCO City of Literature (Arts De
 partment\, Granada City Council) with the University of Granada\nLocation:
  Granada\, Spain. Residency at the Corrala de Santiago\, the University of
  Granada's guest residence.\nAward: Two residencies. Each covers 30 nights
  of accommodation in a single room on a full-board basis at the Corrala de
  Santiago\, plus round-trip travel from the airport nearest the writer's h
 ome to Granada Airport. There is no cash stipend. Transfers between home a
 nd the departure airport\, travel insurance and health insurance are the w
 riter's own responsibility and cost. No application fee.\nDuration: 30 nig
 hts\, Monday 2 November to Tuesday 1 December 2026 inclusive. Deadline 6 S
 eptember 2026\; selected writers announced Thursday 1 October 2026.\n\nMor
 e: https://granadaciudaddeliteratura.com/en/international-granada-writers-
 in-residence-programme-2026/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_med
 ium=referral
URL:https://granadaciudaddeliteratura.com/en/international-granada-writers-
 in-residence-programme-2026/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_med
 ium=referral
LOCATION:Granada\, Spain. Residency at the Corrala de Santiago\, the Univer
 sity of Granada's guest residence.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:vcca-anne-spencer-fellowship-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260901T123517Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260915
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260916
SUMMARY:Deadline: VCCA Anne Spencer Fellowship 2027
DESCRIPTION:Named fellowship at VCCA's Mt. San Angelo campus in rural Virgi
 nia\, established in 2017 in honour of Harlem Renaissance poet and civil r
 ights activist Anne Spencer. It funds a one-month residency plus a USD 1\,
 500 honorarium for writers\, visual artists and composers of African Ameri
 can descent. WHAT YOU GET: private bedroom with private bath\, a separate 
 individual studio away from the bedroom\, and three meals a day\, inside a
  cross-disciplinary community of resident artists\, so the entire cost of 
 being there is carried by VCCA and the honorarium is on top of it. THE ONE
  CATCH ON ELIGIBILITY THIS CYCLE: the fellowship is described as open to w
 riters\, visual artists and composers\, but the 2027 application details n
 arrow the current round to WRITERS\, with preference given to those of Afr
 ican American descent. Read that as a writing-focused cycle rather than an
  open call to all three disciplines. COMMUNITY COMMITMENT: Anne Spencer Fe
 llows tour the Anne Spencer House and Garden Museum in Lynchburg and take 
 part in one Lynchburg-community activity\, choosing between a public prese
